[statement]
A requested name with a single candidate is settled before the request's
other names, whatever their order: `y`, provided by `p2` alone, at no
version and with a priority, is settled first, and `p2` then provides `x`.
A package's own dependency list has no such rule
(`a-name-with-one-candidate-is-not-settled-first-in-a-package`).

[repository]
P:p1
V:1
p:x
k:100

P:p2
V:1
p:x y
k:10

[request]
x
y

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p2 1
